Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["13. Conclusions strictly supported by the notebook", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"d0f4ba79-18f7-5747-bd30-4eb547e46f32"],

Cell["1. The originally stated density", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cfc300ee-c864-1047-87ae-36c6a872b3d9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["L", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "\[Rho]", "log", "\[Chi]", "+", 
         "\[Chi]", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["R", "TI"], "2"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "\\mathcal{L}=\\rho\\log\\chi+\\chi R^2", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cd2c3bd0-8e59-fc4e-9d96-1fe319653cf4"],
 "   is, by itself, an ",
 StyleBox["algebraic",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " variational density and does ",
 StyleBox["not",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 " define a nontrivial PDE field theory without additional derivative \
structure."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"35881474-4349-9648-ae3f-90c5fd395bda"],

Cell["\<\
2. A minimal regularization yields explicit Euler--Lagrange equations that \
can be analyzed symbolically and numerically.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d3f86f6a-fe8d-2e48-ae9a-61c056bb4ebf"],

Cell["\<\
3. Constant-background compatibility is highly restrictive and should be \
checked before any linearized spectral claim is made.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f900265f-38b5-1c40-874b-ab11d57297e1"],

Cell["\<\
4. Stable-frequency claims depend on the actual eigenvalue structure of the \
linearized stiffness matrix and are not automatic.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7df7a87d-28b9-784e-9148-0436ca394c8a"],

Cell["\<\
5. The measurement layer can be made mathematically explicit as a \
projection/integration functional, but physical interpretation requires \
additional assumptions beyond the derivations shown here.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1849ff5d-19cd-6940-9730-0747e245af2c"],

Cell["\<\
6. The notebook provides a reusable audit pipeline from definitions through \
residual verification. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"425acf8f-006e-8c4c-b32c-a45898306869"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {
     TemplateBox[{0},
      "Spacer1"]},
    {
     TemplateBox[{0},
      "Spacer1"]}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   FrameStyle->Directive[
     LightDarkSwitched[
      GrayLevel[0.8], 
      GrayLevel[0.4867756]], 
     AbsoluteThickness[1]],
   GridBoxDividers->{
    "Columns" -> {False, {True}, False}, "Rows" -> {False, {True}, False}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Fit}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Text", "MarkdownDelimiter",
 ShowStringCharacters->False,
 Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"d8b2ebe5-b277-f847-b78d-87def958aaa5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["14. Recommended next rigorous extensions", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"fd922d63-096d-5741-8ef0-bd1826481f49"],

Cell["1. Introduce a precise manifold, metric, and signature.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26ede640-de59-6941-8551-f5289fd4bf67"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "2. State dimensional weights for ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|
    "boxes" -> FormBox["\[Rho]", TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\rho", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5e2b81e8-8fa9-b344-989c-766cbd154934"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|
    "boxes" -> FormBox["\[Chi]", TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\chi", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c742edf2-10b9-9941-85a0-8fa6a6ae7a67"],
 ", and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["R", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "R", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7cb5a467-a8dd-7847-b49b-35585c6f2daf"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"71e2ba96-dc02-6049-a7bc-1750cd1bfd65"],

Cell["\<\
3. Specify whether the intended operator is elliptic, hyperbolic, or mixed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5c3b4641-b8d3-7f42-a203-02e39b98df12"],

Cell["\<\
4. Derive, rather than postulate, any maintenance term from an action or \
semigroup framework.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ae1bf518-d1f1-1947-b3ff-d53b524a0be9"],

Cell["\<\
5. Define admissible function spaces and boundary conditions.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ee6441aa-535f-654c-80f8-ef20ee6a9296"],

Cell["6. Perform Noether analysis after symmetries are fixed.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"336d58d0-8a03-e14e-9489-5f8133403b98"],

Cell["\<\
7. Compare alternative regularizations and prove which properties are \
invariant under that choice.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d0e5a2af-a334-fc40-8aec-f6e3833e1535"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook is intended as a professional mathematical foundation for \
further testing and refinement.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"01f18888-ce1a-074a-9d4d-bb495f1ea8b7"]
}, Open  ]]
},
